    "result_text": "The quick-add bar is in place on the people list, and `bin/e2e` passes all 4 tests: the quick-add test and the three regression scenarios.\n\n**Server**\n- **New endpoint:** `POST /api/sheets/{sheetId}/quick-add` takes `{name, amount}`. The name follows the person form's rules (not blank, at most 200 characters) and the amount follows the claim form's (0.00 or more, up to two decimals). Anything else is refused before anything is stored.\n- **`QuickAddService.add`** runs as one transaction. It looks the person up by trimmed name, ignoring case, so `\" dot \"` matches `Dot`. If nobody matches, it adds the person with grade A through the existing `PersonService.add`. Then it creates the claim through the existing `ClaimService.add` with no date (so it's dated the sheet's today) and an empty note. A new claim is always a draft.\n- **Same rules and audit lines as the forms:** because it reuses those two methods, it writes the existing `PERSON_ADDED` / `ROLLUP` / `CLAIM_ADDED` lines and keeps their checks (duplicate names, closed periods). Both methods join the outer transaction, so if the claim is refused the new person is rolled back too. Audit lines are only written when the transaction commits, so a refusal leaves nothing in the audit file.\n- **One small change to existing code:** I made `ClaimController.ClaimView.of` public so the new controller can use it.\n\n**Front end**\n- **The bar** (`features/people/people.ts`) has `quick-name`, `quick-amount`, `quick-submit` and `quick-error`. A blank name is refused on screen, and server refusals show a message on the bar.\n- **Errors clear** when the bar is edited, submitted again, or the sheet is reloaded.\n- **After a success** the people list is re-read so a newly added person shows up, and the bar is emptied.\n- **`ClaimsService.quickAdd`** puts the new claim at the top of the list, keeping newest first.\n\nThe tests don't cover a quick-add refused for a closed period, which is the \"no new person left behind\" case. I expect it to work because of the shared transaction, but I haven't run it.",
